    "ls|LS16_S7_U_1": "GOVERNMENT OF INDIA \nMINISTRY OF RAILWAYS \n \nLOK SABHA \nSTARRED QUESTION NO. 1 \nTO BE ANSWERED ON 24.02.2016 \n \nRAILWAY REGULATORY AUTHORITY \n \n \n*1.      SHRI PRALHAD JOSHI:  \n           SHRI B. VINOD KUMAR:   \n \n    Will the Minister of RAILWAYS be pleased to state: \n \n(a) whether the Government proposes to set up an independent \nregulatory authority for the Indian Railways as envisaged in the \nReport of the Committee for Mobilisation of Resources for Major \nRailway Projects and Restructuring of Railway Ministry and \nRailway Board; \n \n(b) if so, the likely terms of reference, composition, along with \npowers and functions of the Authority; and \n \n(c) the details of progress made in this regard? \n \n \n \nANSWER \n \n \nMINISTER OF RAILWAYS \n \n(SHRI SURESH PRABHAKAR PRABHU) \n \n \n(a) to (c): A Statement is laid on the Table of the House. \n \n***** \n\nSTATEMENT REFERRED TO IN REPLY TO PARTS (a) TO (c) OF \nSTARRED QUESTION NO. 1 BY SHRI PRALHAD JOSHI AND SHRI B.  \nVINOD KUMAR TO BE ANSWERED IN LOK SABHA ON 24.02.2016 \nREGARDING RAILWAY REGULATORY AUTHORITY \n \n(a) to (c): In the Rail Budget 2015 -16, setting up of a mechanism for \nmaking regulations, setting performance standards, determining \ntariffs and dispute resolution was announced. In December 2015, \nMinistry of Railways brought out for public consul tation a concept \npaper on regulatory framework and setting up of Rail Development \nAuthority of India. The concept paper envisages that the Authority \nwill: \n \n(i) Protect consumer interest, promote competition and \nencourage market development.  \n(ii) Undertake functions of tariff determination, ensuring fair \nplay & level playing field for private investments, setting \nefficiency & performance standards and dissemination of \ninformation.  \n(iii) Consist of Chairman and four other Members who have \nspecial knowled ge of and professional experience in \nrailways, infrastructure, finance, law and management or \nconsumer affairs.       \n \n***** \n \n \n ",
    "ls|LS16_S7_U_10": " \n \nGOVERNMENT OF INDIA \nMINISTRY OF RAILWAYS \n \nLOK   SABHA \nSTARRED QUESTION NO.10 \nTO BE ANSWERED ON 24.02.2016 \n    \nSHORTAGE OF COACHES \n \n*10.   SHRI V. ELUMALAI: \n          SHRI JAGDAMBIKA PAL:   \n \n Will the Minister of RAILWAYS be pleased to state: \n(a) whether any  policy/ guidelines/ standard operating procedure has \nbeen drawn with respect to standards of coaches and wagons in \nthe Railways, if so, the details thereof;  \n \n(b) whether the standard of coaches of long distance trains are \ngenerally not commensurate with the travelling distance, as most \nof them are refurbished old coaches; \n \n(c) if so, the details thereof; \n \n(d) whether short distance trains are provided with new coaches, and \nif so, the reasons therefor; \n \n(e) whether the Southern Zonal railways is facing acute shortage of \ncoaches and the projected demand of coaches hardly met; and  \n \n(f) if so, the details thereof along with the reasons therefor and the \nremedial action being taken in the matter? \n \nANSWER \nMINISTER OF RAILWAYS \n(SHRI SURESH PRABHAKAR PRABHU) \n(a) to (f): A Statement is laid on the Table of the House. \n***** \n \n \n\n \n \n \nSTATEMENT REFERRED TO IN REPLY TO PARTS (a) TO (f) OF \nSTARRED QUESTION NO. 10 BY SHRI V. ELUMALAI  AND SHRI \nJAGDAMBIKA PAL TO BE ANSWERED IN LOK SABHA ON 24.02.2016 \nREGARDING SHORTAGE OF COACHES.  \n \n(a):  Coaches and wagons are used in train service only if they are \nfit as per laid down standards. \n \n(b):   No, Madam. \n \n(c):   Does not arise. \n \n(d):  No, Madam. All trains are attached with coaches after being \nproperly examined and found fit. \n \n(e) & (f):   No, Madam. Presently, adequate numbers of coaches have \nbeen provided to all zonal railways including Southern Railway for \nrunning passenger carrying trains to their scheduled compositions \nwhich is considered sufficient for the present level of traffic. During \nthe cur rent financial year, the production of coaches is \ncommensurate with the projected requirement as planned. \n***** ",
    "ls|LS16_S7_U_100": "������������������� �\n�������������������� �\n�\n��������� �\n��������������������� ���� �\n���������������������������� �\n�\n��������������������������������������� �\n�\n���������������� ������������������� ��\n�\n����������������������������������������������������� �\n���\n����������� ����� ����������� ���� �������� ��� �������� �����������\n����������������������������������������������� �\n�\n��������������������������������\n�������������������������������������������������������������������\n���������������������������������������������������������� ���������\n��������������� �\n���� ��� ���� �������� ���� ����������� ��� ������� ��� ���� ���� ���� ����� ���\n������� ����� ����� ���������� ����� ��� ���������� ���������� ��� ����\n��������������������������������������� �\n������ �\n��������������������������������������������� �\n��������� ��������� �\n���������������������������������������������������������������������\n�������� ������� �������� ��������� ������������ ������������ �����\n��������������������������������������������������������������������\n����������� ������������ ��� ����� ���� ���� ������ ��� ���� ������� ����\n�������� ������������������������������������������� �\n��������\n�\n\n����\n��������� ������ ����� ���������� ��� ����������� �������� �������� ���\n������ ���� ������� � ���� ������� ����� ���� �������������� ���\n����������������������������������������������������������������\n�������������������������������������������������������������������\n��� ���� ����� ������� ��� ���� ���� ��������������������� ��� ����\n������������������������������� �\n�\n���� �",
    "ls|LS16_S7_U_101": "�\n������������������� �\n�������������������� �\n�\n��������� �\n����������������������� � � � �\n������������������ �� �� � ���� � �\n�\n����������������������������������� �\n�\n�\n�� � � ��� ������������������ �\n�\n�\n�\n�������������������������������������������������� �\n�\n�\n����� ��� � �������� ��� ���� �������� ������ ������������� ��������� ���\n�������������������� ������ �\n�\n����� �������� ���� �������������� ��� �������� ����� ������� ������ ���\n����������������������� �\n�\n����� ��� ���� ���� �������� �������� ���� ���� ������ ������ ��� ������ ����\n������������ �\n�\n�\n����� � �\n��������������������������������������������� �\n������������������ �\n�\n�\n�\n����������������������������������������������������������� �\n��\n��\n�\n�������\n� �",
    "ls|LS16_S7_U_104": "GOVERNMENT OF INDIA \nMINISTRY OF STATISTICS AND PROGRAMME IMPLEMENTATION \n \nLOK SABHA  \nUNSTARRED QUESTION NO. 104 \nTO BE ANSWERED ON WEDNESDAY, 24TH FEBRUARY, 2016 \n \nDATABASE OF MINORITIES \n \n104.    SHRI ARVIND SAWANT: \n   SHRI KRUPAL BALAJI TUMANE:  \n    \n        Will the Minister of STATISTICS AND PROGRAMME \nIMPLEMENTATION be pleased to state: \n \n(a) whether any database in regard to social -religious categories of \nminorities is available/has been prepared;  \n(b) if so, the details thereof; \n(c) the steps taken by the Government to prepare a National Data \nBank in regard to the social-religious categories of M inorities; \nand  \n(d) the amount likely to be spent on preparation of such a data \nbank? \n \n \nANSWER \n \nMINISTER OF STATE (INDEPENDENT CHARGE) FOR MINISTRY OF \nSTATISTICS AND PROGRAMME IMPLEMENTATION AND MINISTER OF \nSTATE FOR MINISTRY OF EXTERNAL AFFAIRS [GENERAL (Dr.) V. K. \nSINGH (Retd.)] \n \n(a)&(b):  National Data Bank for Socio -Religious Categories has been \nprepared and link is available in the Ministry’s website (mospi.gov.in).  \n \n(c)&(d):  There is no proposal at present to prepare a National Data \nBank in regard to the social-religious categories of Minorities. \n***** ",
    "ls|LS16_S7_U_105": " \nGOVERNMENT OF INDIA \nMINISTRY OF RAILWAYS \n \nLOK SABHA \nUNSTARRED QUESTION NO.105 \nTO BE ANSWERED ON 24.02.2016 \n \nLOADING PARCELS IN TRAINS \n \n 105. SHRI YOGI ADITYA NATH: \n \nWill the Minister of RAILWAYS be pleased to state: \n \n(a) whether parcels are loaded in trains at the railway stations without \nchecking; and \n \n(b) if so, the details thereof and the reaction of the Government thereto? \n \n \nANSWER  \n \nMINISTER OF STATE IN THE MINISTRY OF RAILWAYS \n \n(SHRI MANOJ SINHA) \n \n(a) & (b): Parcels for booking and carriage by rail are acc epted from the \nsender/consignor on execution of forwarding note by him as prescribed \nunder Railway Act, 1989. Consignor is solely responsible for the \ncorrectness of the entries made by him in the forwarding note. When \nParcels are offered for booking, these  are carefully examined by the \nRailway staff.  In  case of any doubt, contents of packages can be \nchecked by Railway staff. In addition to this, regular as well as surprise \nchecks are conducted by Commercial, Vigilance and Railway Protection \nForce personnel to check the contents of the packages.  In case of any \nmisdeclaration of contents of the packages, action is taken as per rules. \n***** ",
    "ls|LS16_S7_U_108": "GOVERNMENT OF INDIA \nMINISTRY OF WATER RESOURCES, \nRIVER DEVELOPMENT & GANGA REJUVENATION \nLOK SABHA \nSTARRED QUESTION NO. †*108 \nANSWERED ON 03.03.2016 \n \nPOLLUTED RIVER STRETCHES \n  \n†*108.         SHRI DHARMENDRA YADAV \n        SHRI SHRIRANG APPA BARNE \n \nWill the  Minister of WATER RESOURCES, RIVER DEVELOPMENT AND GANGA \nREJUVENATION be pleased to state: \n \n(a) whether the Government is aware that besides river Ganga, 254 other polluted river stretches too \nrequire attention towards cleaning, if so, the details thereof;  \n(b) whether the Central Pollution Control Board (CPCB) has found that the number of such stretches \nhave increased to 302 in 2015 from 150 in 2009, if so, the facts thereof;  \n(c) whether her Ministry has studied the observations of CPCB and if so, the outcome thereof;  \n(d) whether as many as 532 towns/cities fall along the polluted stretches of different rivers across the \ncountry and the Municipal Corporations are not able to t reat increased load of sewage flowing into the \nwater bodies; and  \n(e) if so, the details thereof and the action taken/to be taken by the Government in this regard? \n \nANSWER \nTHE MINISTER OF STATE IN THE MINISTRY OF WATER RESOURCES, RIVER \nDEVELOPMENT AND GANGA REJUVENATION   (SUSHRI UMA BHARTI) \n \n(a) to (e)       A Statement is laid on the Table of the House. \n\nStatement referred to in reply to parts (a) to (e) of Lok Sabha Starred Question No.108to be answered on \nThursday, the 3rdMarch, 2016 on “ Polluted River Stretches”raised by SHRI DHARMENDRA YADAV: SHRI \nSHRIRANG APPA BARNE \n \n \n(a)& (b) Yes, Madam. The Government is aware that there are several other river stretches other than river Ganga. In \nfact, based on the water quality assessment conducted Central Pollution Control Board (CPCB), CPCB had identified \n150 river stretches as polluted on 121 rivers in the country during 2008. During 2015, the s tatus was re-assessed and \n302 river stretches identified as polluted on 275 rivers in the country including river Ganga; and communicated to \nState Pollution Control Boards for preparing action plan for restoration of these river stretches. \n(c) to (e) Yes, Madam. The Government has studied the CPCB report.The Government  has formulated river action \nplans to restore water quality of rivers through the Ministry for Water Resources for river Ganga and its tributaries, and \nthrough the Ministry of Environment and Climate Change for all other rivers. The river action plans have been taken \nup on  rivers through State Governments to intercept, divert and treatment of municipal wastewater from urban centers \nwhich is not been able to adequately handle the complete sewage treatment. \nThere are 650 towns along the 302 polluted river stretches identified on 275 rivers. Out of 46 metropolitan cities \n(Census 2011), 35 cities are located along the polluted river stretches. \nThe state-wise number of towns/cities in descending order are – Maharashtra (161), Assam (49), West Bengal (46), \nGujarat (38), Madhya Pradesh (37), Uttar Prad esh (37), Karnataka (24), Kerala (22), Tamil Nadu (23), Odisha (20), \nRajasthan (20), Jammu & Kashmir (18), Manipur (17), Telangana (18), Jharkhand (16), Himachal Pradesh (14), \nChhattisgarh (12), Meghalaya (12), Sikkim (11), Goa (9), Andhra Pradesh (8), Bihar (8), Haryana (7), Uttarakhand (6), \nNagaland (4), Tripura (4), Punjab (5), Daman & Diu (2), Delhi (1). \nOut of 46 metropolitan cities  (Census 2011),   35 cities (Vijayawada, Patna, Raipur, Delhi, Ahmedabad, Surat, \nVadodara, Srinagar, Dhanbad, Ranchi, Bangalore, Indore, Bhopal, Jabalpur, Mumbai, Pune, Nagpur, Thane, Pimpri -\nChinchwad, Nashik, Kalyan -Dombivali, Vasai -Virar, Ludhiana, Kota, Hyderabad, Lucknow, Kanpur, Ghaziabad, \nAgra, Meerut, Varanasi, Allahabad, Kolkata, Howrah, Faridabad) are identified along the polluted river stretches. \nCPCB estimated the sewage generation in Class I & Class- II towns during 2008 and assessed that there was a gap of \n27000 MLD between the sewage.  The sewage generated and treated and   sewage generation is linked to the \npopulation growth especially in urban centers. There was a GAP of around 27000 MLD. The updated information on \nthe sewage generation and treatment capacity developed indicates a GAP in treatment of about 38000 MLD during \n2015 due to inadequate facility for sewage treatment. \nIn the 11 Ganga Basin States, the Consortium of IITs have estimated  that 12050 mld of sewage is generated from \nClass-I &II towns.  7301 mld is generated from the 175 Class I and 102 Class II towns of 5 Ganga basin states on the \nmain stem of  river Ganga namely, Uttarakhand, Uttar Pradesh, Bihar, Jharkhand and West Bengal. The available \ntreatment capacity is about 2125 mld. In addition, STPs for a treatment capacity of about 1188 mld are under \nconstruction / approval, thus leaving a gap of about 3988 mld in this 5 basin states.  \nUnder NGRBA till December 2015, 34 nos. of STPs in Ganga and 03 nos. of STP in Yamuna of total capacity 808.23 \nMLD have been sanctioned. \n \nCPCB has given directions to Municipal authorities/corporations under section 5 of the Environment (Protection) Act,  \n1986 for treatment and utilization of sewage for restoration of water quality of rivers. \n***** ",
    "ls|LS16_S7_U_109": "������������������� �\n���������������������������� �\n�\n��������� �\n�������������������� � ���� �\n����������������������������� �\n�\n�������������������� �\n�\n���� � � ����������������� ��\n� � ����������������������� �����\n���������������� ��\n� ���\n� ���������������������������������������������������������� �\n�\n���� �������� ���� ����������� ���� ������� ������������ ��������� ����� ��������\n����������� �\n�\n���� ��� ���� ���� �������� ��������� ��� ������������ ����� ������� ���������� ���\n��������\n�\n���� �������������������������� ����������������������������������� �\n�\n���� ��������������������������������������������� �\n�\n������ �\n��������������������������������������������������������� �\n�������� � ��������������������� �\n�\n����� ��� ��� ������� ������ ���� ������������ ��������� ��� ������ ����� ��� ����������\n������� ����������� ��������� ������������ ��������� ��������� �������� ����������\n�������� ������� ������� �������� ��������� ����� ������ ����������� ��������\n���������� ����������� �������� ���������� �� ����� ������������� ������ ��������\n���������� ��������� ��� ������� �������� ������ �������� ������ �������� �������\n������������� ������������ ���������� ��������� �������� ����� ���� ��������� �����\n������������������������ �\n�\n����� ��� ����� ���������� ��� ��������� ���� ������������ ��� �� ������� ��� ���� �\n������� ���������� ��� ������� �������� ������ ����� ��� ������� ������ ������ ������\n���������������� �������� ��� ����������� ��� ����� ���� �������� �������� �����\n��������������������������������������������������������������������������\n�������� ��� ������ ����� ��� ����� ���� �������� �������� ������ ������� �� ��������\n������������� ������� ������ ���������� ���� ������ ���������� ������������� �������\n����������������������������������������������������� �\n�\n����������� ����������������������������������������������������� ����� �������\n��� ������� ���� ������� ����� ���� ��� ������������� ��� ���� ���������� ����� �����\n������������������������������������������������������������������������ �\n����� �\n�",
    "ls|LS16_S7_U_110": "������������������� �\n�������������������� ������������������� �\n�\n��������� �\n������� �������������� ����\n������������ ��� �������� ������\n�\n����������� �\n�\n������������������������������ �\n�\n������������������������������������������������� �\n���������������������������������������������������� \n�\n���������������������\n�\n����������������������������������������������������������������������������������������������\n�����������������������������������������������������������������������������������������\n�\n������������������������������������������������������������������������������������������������\n����������������������\n�\n����������������������������������������������������������������������������������������\n�\n������������ ���� ����������� ���� ���������� ��� ��������� ��� �������� ��� ������������\n��������������������������������������\n�\n�����������������������������������������������������������������������������������������������\n�\n�\n������ �\n�\n������������������������������������������� �\n��������������������������� �\n��� ����������������������������������������������������������\n\n�������� ������������������������������������������������������������\n�������� �������� ����� ������������� ��� ��������� ������ ��� ���������\n����������� ����������� ������������ �\n����� �����������������������������������������������������������������������������������\n������� ����� ��������� ������� ���������� ���� ������������������ ������������������ ����������\n������� ���������������� �������� ��� ����������� ������� ������� ��� ������ ���������� ���������\n��������� ���� ����������� ���� ���� ������������� ���������������� ��������������� �������������� ���������������� ���������������\n����������������������������������������������������������������������������������������������\n��� �������� ��� ������� ���������� ����� ��� ���������� ������� �������� �� �������������� ����\n����������������������������������������������������������������������������������������������\n�����������������������������\n���� ����������������� ��� ����� ���������� �� ��������� ��� ����������� ��������� ���������� ����\n�������������������������������������������������������������������\n������\n�\n�",
    "ls|LS16_S7_U_111": "GOVERNMENT OF INDIA \nMINISTRY OF RAILWAYS \n \nLOK SABHA \nUNSTARRED QUESTION NO.111 \nTO BE ANSWERED ON 24.02.2016 \n \nLHB COACHES \n \n111. SHRI SHRIRANG APPA BARNE: \n        SHRI ANANDRAO ADSUL:  \n        SHRI DHARMENDRA YADAV:  \n        SHRI P.R. SUNDARAM:  \n        SHRI ADHALRAO PATIL SHIVAJIRAO: \n \n  Will the Minister of RAILWAYS be pleased to state: \n \n(a) whether the Railways took a decision to replace the conventional AC and \nnon-AC coaches with new Linke Hofmann Busch (LHB) coaches in all trains \nby the end of 2016; \n \n(b) if so, whether while passengers complain of rattling and unclean coaches \nin many express/passenger trains, whereas LHB coaches; \n \n(c) if so, the number of coaches procured and number out of them have not \nbeen utilised so far along with the reasons therefor;  \n \n(d) whether the LHB coaches have not been allocated to the zones as per \ntheir size or as per their requirement and if so, the reasons therefor; and \n \n(e) the steps taken by the Government to use these LHB coaches and \nprovide more LHB coaches in high spe ed trains under the Southern \nRailways? \nANSWER \nMINISTER OF STATE IN THE MINISTRY OF RAILWAYS \n(SHRI MANOJ SINHA) \n(a) No, Madam.  \n \n(b) Does not arise. \n\n \n(c) to (e) About 3300 LHB coaches have been made available from \nproduction units for the purpose of utilization as new service as well as \nreplacement. Production and the allotment of coaches is an ongoing \nprocess. Allocations of LHB coaches to all zonal Railways including Southern \nRailway are being done keeping in view the production, requirement and \ninfrastructure for maintaining LHB coaches available at Zonal Railway.  \n \n***** ",
    "ls|LS16_S7_U_112": "GOVERNMENT OF INDIA \nMINISTRY OF HOUSING AND URBAN POVERTY ALLEVIATION \nLOK SABHA \nUNSTARRED QUESTION NO. 112 \nTO BE ANSWERED ON FEBRUARY 24, 2016 \n \nSKILL TRAINING FOR POOR \n \nNo. 112 SHRI S.P.MUDDAHANUME GOWDA:   \n   \nWill the Minister of HOUSING AN D URBAN POVERTY ALLEVIATION \nbe pleased to state:- \n(a) whether the Government is making any efforts through \nimparting skill to make the urban  poor eligible for gainful \nemployment or undertake wage employment; \n(b) if so, the details thereof; \n(c) whether the Government is focusing on SCs/STs in urban areas \nso that they can become eligib le for gainful employment or \nundertake wage employment; \n(d) if so, the details thereof; and  \n(e) if not, the reasons therefor? \n \nANSWER \nTHE MINISTER OF STATE IN  \nTHE MINISTRY OF HOUSING & URBAN POVERTY ALLEVIATION \n[SHRI BABUL SUPRIYO] \n  \n(a) & (b): The Ministry of Housing and Urban Poverty \nAlleviation is implementing a Centrally Sponsored Scheme \n“Deendayal Antyodaya Yojana — National Urban Livelihoods \nMission”. The Employment through Skill Training & Placement \n(EST&P) component of the Missi on aims at providing skill \ntraining to urban poor so that they can find gainful \nemployment or set up self-emp loyment ventures or secure \nwage employment.   \n(c)  to (e): As per Mission guide lines, SCs and ST s are to be \nbenefited at least to the exten t of the proportion of their \npopulation in the city. \n****** \n ",
    "ls|LS16_S7_U_113": " \n \n                                          GOVERNMENT OF INDIA \n                                         MINISTRY OF RAILWAYS \n                      LOK SABHA \n                                    UNSTARRED QUESTION NO.113 \n                                   TO BE ANSWERED ON 24.02.2016 \n \n \n                        SETTING UP OF RAIL COACH FACTORY \n \n   113. SHRI RAJESH KUMAR DIWAKER: \n    \n   Will the Minister of RAILWAYS be pleased to state: \n    \n(a) whether the  Railways proposes to set up a rail coach factory in Hathras \n(UP); \n \n(b) if so, the details thereof;     \n \n(c) the funds required for setting up the said factory along with the pattern of \nits funding; \n \n(d) whether necessary clearances have been obtained for the project from the \nState Government and other agencies and if so, the details thereof and \nresponse of State; \n \n(e) whether the site of the factory has been identified and land allotted for the \npurpose; and \n \n(f) if not, the time by which it is likely to be allotted and which type of coaches \nproposes to be manufactured in the said factory? \n \n \nANSWER \n \nMINISTER OF STATE IN THE MINISTRY OF RAILWAYS \n \n                                      (SHRI MANOJ SINHA) \n \n(a) No, Madam. \n \n(b)  to (f) Do not arise. \n***** ",
